WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.266 --> 00:00:01.334 align:start size:94% position:6%
-Well, you know,
"The Good Place,"

00:00:01.334 --> 00:00:02.035 size:75% position:38% line:92%
again, was a show --

00:00:02.035 --> 00:00:03.136 align:start size:94% position:6%
and I know when everybody
auditioned for it,

00:00:03.136 --> 00:00:05.271 align:start size:94% position:6%
it was fake scripts, because
unlike a lot of sitcoms,

00:00:05.271 --> 00:00:07.440 align:start size:94% position:6%
you know, there were
a lot of turns in the show

00:00:07.440 --> 00:00:09.409 line:92%
a lot of cliffhanger endings

00:00:09.409 --> 00:00:12.012
When you knew you were doing
the show in the very beginning

00:00:12.012 --> 00:00:13.413 align:start size:94% position:6%
did you have trouble
explaining it to people?

00:00:13.413 --> 00:00:17.851 align:start size:94% position:6%
Were you worried you were gonn
tip off what the idea was?

00:00:17.851 --> 00:00:19.586 align:start size:94% position:6% line:92%
-You're outing me.

00:00:19.586 --> 00:00:22.555
Yeah, it was like -- if you have
seen it, if you haven't,

00:00:22.555 --> 00:00:25.425 align:start size:94% position:6%
there's a big twist
at the end of the first episod

00:00:25.425 --> 00:00:28.094 align:start size:94% position:6%
where you think I'm workin
for the God Squad,

00:00:28.094 --> 00:00:30.497 align:start size:94% position:6%
and really I am a demon
torturing them.

00:00:30.497 --> 00:00:32.499 align:start size:94% position:6%
-Yeah.
-And it was a great flip

00:00:32.499 --> 00:00:35.335 align:start size:94% position:6%
that really got everyone
energized who was watching it.

00:00:35.335 --> 00:00:38.605 align:start size:94% position:6%
So we were told,
"Please do not tell anybody.

00:00:38.605 --> 00:00:40.473 align:start size:94% position:6%
In fairness,
they said that after

00:00:40.473 --> 00:00:42.542
what I'm about to describe
-You told a bunch of people.

00:00:42.542 --> 00:00:44.644 align:start size:94% position:6%
-I went to --
you know John Krasinksi.

00:00:44.644 --> 00:00:46.112 align:start size:94% position:6%
-Wonderful guy.
-Wonderful guy,

00:00:46.112 --> 00:00:49.416
and worked with Mike Shore
as well, on "The Office."

00:00:49.416 --> 00:00:51.051 align:start size:94% position:6%
And I'm a little
competitive with him.

00:00:51.051 --> 00:00:54.621
I only compete with people who
I can't possibly ever win with

00:00:54.621 --> 00:00:56.122 align:start size:94% position:6%
-Yeah, yeah.
-I find that more...

00:00:56.122 --> 00:00:58.558
stimulating or something.
I don't know. So, I was --

00:00:58.558 --> 00:01:02.729 align:start size:94% position:6%
I'm very competitive with John
in this great way, and I -

00:01:02.729 --> 00:01:04.531 align:start size:94% position:6%
He's going off
to make a big action movie

00:01:04.531 --> 00:01:05.932 align:start size:94% position:6%
and he said,
"What are you doing?"

00:01:05.932 --> 00:01:07.133 align:start size:94% position:6%
And I went,
"Oh, I'm about to work

00:01:07.133 --> 00:01:09.202 align:start size:94% position:6%
with one of your buddies,
Mike Shore,"

00:01:09.202 --> 00:01:11.871 align:start size:94% position:6%
and I play, kind of,
middle management

00:01:11.871 --> 00:01:14.574 align:start size:94% position:6%
in 'The Good Place,'
it's called,

00:01:14.574 --> 00:01:15.575 align:start size:94% position:6% line:92%
in the afterlife."

00:01:15.575 --> 00:01:16.609 line:92%
And I could see his eyes go,

00:01:16.609 --> 00:01:19.345 align:start size:94% position:6%
"Oh, yeah, 'The Office,'
but in heaven.

00:01:19.345 --> 00:01:20.480 line:92%
Yeah, I got it. I got it."

00:01:20.480 --> 00:01:21.147 align:start size:94% position:6% line:92%
[ Laughter ]

00:01:21.147 --> 00:01:24.384 align:start size:94% position:6%
And I went
"No, [mumbles]. No.

00:01:24.384 --> 00:01:26.586 align:start size:94% position:6%
It turns out that
I'm actually a demon

00:01:26.586 --> 00:01:27.654 line:92%
at the end of the first season."

00:01:27.654 --> 00:01:30.457 align:start size:94% position:6%
And I saw him light up and go,
"Oh, that's interesting."

00:01:30.457 --> 00:01:32.325 align:start size:94% position:6% line:92%
I go, "Yeah!"

00:01:32.325 --> 00:01:34.094 align:start size:94% position:6% line:92%
[ Laughter ]

00:01:34.094 --> 00:01:36.996 align:start size:94% position:6%
Uh, I want to ask you abou
"Curb," which is so fantastic,

00:01:36.996 --> 00:01:38.598 align:start size:94% position:6%
'cause you play
yourself on "Curb,"

00:01:38.598 --> 00:01:40.366 align:start size:94% position:6%
and I know Larry's
a dear friend of yours,

00:01:40.366 --> 00:01:43.036 align:start size:94% position:6%
so it must, at times,
just not feel like work at all

00:01:43.036 --> 00:01:45.105 align:start size:94% position:6%
-Correct.
-Yet he did something very -

00:01:45.105 --> 00:01:46.239 align:start size:94% position:6%
very cruel...
-Yeah, yeah.

00:01:46.239 --> 00:01:48.041 align:start size:94% position:6%
-...which is he made
you and Mary --

00:01:48.041 --> 00:01:50.276 align:start size:94% position:6%
on "Curb,"
you guys are divorced.

00:01:50.276 --> 00:01:53.146 align:start size:94% position:6%
-Yeah.
-Yeah.

00:01:53.146 --> 00:01:54.547 align:start size:94% position:6%
-And we would get --
we'd get calls

00:01:54.547 --> 00:01:58.318
from friends we'd had dinner
with, like, a month before

00:01:58.318 --> 00:02:00.120 align:start size:94% position:6% line:92%
going, "Oh..."

00:02:00.120 --> 00:02:01.554 align:start size:94% position:6% line:92%
[ Laughter ]

00:02:01.554 --> 00:02:02.655 line:92%
You know, you felt like saying

00:02:02.655 --> 00:02:05.525 align:start size:94% position:6%
"Yeah, yeah,
all big, serious events,

00:02:05.525 --> 00:02:08.761 align:start size:94% position:6%
we like to announce
on the Larry David show."

00:02:08.761 --> 00:02:09.395 align:start size:94% position:6% line:92%
-Yeah.

00:02:09.395 --> 00:02:11.197 align:start size:94% position:6%
Well, he's -- of all
your friends, he's the most --

00:02:11.197 --> 00:02:13.466 align:start size:94% position:6%
You know, he's the most
emotionally connected, Larry

00:02:13.466 --> 00:02:15.001 align:start size:94% position:6%
If you had a big divorce
in your life,

00:02:15.001 --> 00:02:16.603 align:start size:94% position:6%
you would definitely want
Larry to tell people.

00:02:16.603 --> 00:02:19.806
-You know, actually,
Mary once said to him, you know,

00:02:19.806 --> 00:02:20.707 line:92%
"If I was ever in real trouble

00:02:20.707 --> 00:02:22.976
you'd be one of the first people
I would call,"

00:02:22.976 --> 00:02:24.511 line:92%
and it almost made him cry

00:02:24.511 --> 00:02:26.546 align:start size:94% position:6%
-Really?
-Yes, and she meant it.

00:02:26.546 --> 00:02:27.747 align:start size:94% position:6%
-Really?
-Go figure.

00:02:27.747 --> 00:02:29.215 align:start size:94% position:6%
-Wow.
-He would be the last person..

00:02:29.215 --> 00:02:32.519 align:start size:94% position:6%
-I would -- and I can't believ
his reaction was crying

00:02:32.519 --> 00:02:33.386 line:92%
and not him saying, like,

00:02:33.386 --> 00:02:36.222 align:start size:94% position:6%
"I don't want you to call me."
-I know, right, yes.

00:02:36.222 --> 00:02:38.992 align:start size:94% position:6%
Well, he was caught off guard.
-Yeah.

00:02:38.992 --> 00:02:41.427 align:start size:94% position:6%
One piece of really exciting
news, which is, it's sad.

00:02:41.427 --> 00:02:44.230
"The Good Place" is coming
to a close, but you, uh --

00:02:44.230 --> 00:02:46.533 align:start size:94% position:6%
You already have
your next show lined up.

00:02:46.533 --> 00:02:47.233 align:start size:94% position:6% line:92%
-Yes, yes, yes.

00:02:47.233 --> 00:02:49.002 align:start size:94% position:6%
You're doing a show on NBC
with Tina Fey...

00:02:49.002 --> 00:02:50.270 align:start size:94% position:6%
-Tina Fey.
-...as the creator,

00:02:50.270 --> 00:02:52.238 align:start size:94% position:6%
and Robert Carlock,
her great partner.

00:02:52.238 --> 00:02:54.707 align:start size:94% position:6%
-Right, actually
I've spent some time with them

00:02:54.707 --> 00:02:57.277 align:start size:94% position:6%
Everyone says
"Tina Fey and Robert Carlock."

00:02:57.277 --> 00:02:58.645 align:start size:94% position:6%
-Yeah.
-It's Robert Carlock.

00:02:58.645 --> 00:03:00.880 align:start size:94% position:6%
-He's just -- I've known him
a long time.

00:03:00.880 --> 00:03:02.715 line:92%
Yeah, I would say they're equal,

00:03:02.715 --> 00:03:05.185 align:start size:94% position:6%
because I'm afraid
of both of them.

00:03:05.185 --> 00:03:06.986 align:start size:94% position:6%
Yeah, so I like
to put them equal pedestals.

00:03:06.986 --> 00:03:08.655 align:start size:94% position:6%
-I know for a fact
they don't watch your show

00:03:08.655 --> 00:03:10.256 line:92%
so that's why I could say that

00:03:10.256 --> 00:03:12.192 align:start size:94% position:6% line:92%
[ Laughter ]

00:03:12.192 --> 00:03:15.261 align:start size:94% position:6%
-Well, there's no way I'm gonn
beat that for a closer.

00:03:15.261 --> 00:03:17.397 size:78% position:39% line:92%
Ted Danson, everyone.

